#!/usr/bin/env stryke
## benches/bench_keyboard_keys.stk — FFI round-trip micro-bench.
##
## `GUI::keyboard_keys()` is the cheapest path through the `gui` cdylib
## (no enigo init, no OS permissions, no JSON args — just a JSON dump of
## a static key-name slice). Calling it in a tight `bench { ... } N`
## block measures the cost of one stryke → cdylib → JSON → stryke
## round-trip.
##
## Discovered by `s bench` (matches the `bench_*.stk` naming convention).
## Compare against the `bench { 1 + 1 } 1000` baseline in
## strykelang/examples/project/lib/benchmarks.stk to attribute cost to
## the FFI boundary vs raw stryke dispatch.

use GUI

p "GUI::keyboard_keys (FFI roundtrip):"
p bench { GUI::keyboard_keys() } 1000

p "raw stryke baseline (1+1):"
p bench { 1 + 1 } 1000
